---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions — Finora"
  description="Finora Terms & Conditions. Read about usage terms, data sources, and limitations."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <div>
      <p class="font-mono text-caption-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">// legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-display-lg text-ink">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-mute">Last updated: August 28, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose mt-10 space-y-8 text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using Finora (the "Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms &amp; Conditions.
          If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">2. Nature of the Service</h2>
        <p>
          Finora is a financial research and information tool. It reads publicly available financial data —
          primarily from SEC EDGAR filings — and computes standard financial metrics using deterministic algorithms.
          The Service is designed to help users understand public company financials more efficiently.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">3. Not Investment Advice</h2>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Finora does not provide investment advice, recommendations, or opinions
          about the value of any security or the suitability of any investment.</strong> Nothing on the Service
          should be construed as an offer to buy or sell, or a solicitation of an offer to buy or sell,
          any security. You should consult a qualified financial advisor before making any investment decisions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">4. No Brokerage Relationship</h2>
        <p>
          Use of Finora does not create a broker-client, advisor-client, or any other fiduciary relationship
          between you and Finora Labs or its affiliates.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">5. Data Sources &amp; Accuracy</h2>
        <p>
          Finora derives financial data from public sources including SEC EDGAR XBRL filings, company
          investor relations materials, and third-party market data providers. While we strive for accuracy,
          <strong class="text-ink">you should independently verify all material information</strong> before
          relying on it for any purpose. Financial data may contain errors, omissions, or timing differences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">6. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          Finora relies on third-party APIs and services (including but not limited to SEC EDGAR, Twelve Data,
          Tavily, Jina, and NVIDIA) to provide its features. These external services may become unavailable,
          change their terms, or modify their APIs without notice. Finora is not responsible for the
          availability, accuracy, or policies of third-party services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">7. Service Availability</h2>
        <p>
          Finora makes no guarantee of uninterrupted or error-free service. The Service may be temporarily
          unavailable due to maintenance, technical issues, or factors beyond our control.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">8. Usage Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          Research runs and chat messages are subject to usage limits. Finora reserves the right to modify
          usage limits at any time. Automated scraping, bulk extraction, or abuse of the Service is prohibited.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">9. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          The Finora platform, design, and algorithms are proprietary to Finora Labs. SEC data and public
          filing content are in the public domain. You may not copy, redistribute, or reverse-engineer
          the Service's proprietary components.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">10. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 pl-4">
          <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose</li>
          <li>Attempt to circumvent usage limits or security measures</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Service</li>
          <li>Impersonate any person or entity</li>
          <li>Use automated tools to extract data at scale without authorization</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">11. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Finora Labs and its affiliates shall not be liable for
          any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of
          the Service, including but not limited to investment losses, data inaccuracies, or service interruptions.
          The Service is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">12. Changes to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated
          date. Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Contact us at
          <a href="mailto:hello@finora.dev" class="text-accent hover:underline">hello@finora.dev</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
